  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Some viral content on the internet starts spreading through an audience of $60\\,000$ people. The rate of growth in the number of people $P(t)$ who have seen the content is jointly proportional to the number of people who have seen the content at time $t,$ measured in hours, and the number who have not. If the constant of proportionality is $0.75,$ which differential equation could be used to model $P(t)?$",
